    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 84.03 score, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Bibee. His combination of batting leadoff and a strong platoon advantage against the right-hander makes him our primary anchor for both counting stats and stolen base potential. **Mickey Moniak** also projects as a high-upside play at 75.75; his score is significantly bolstered by a 14% park factor boost and a prime spot in the two-hole, making him a dangerous asset against Wacha. Additionally, **Brice Turang** earns a strong 73.40 rating by exploiting a soft matchup against Johnson, where his leadoff status and the pitcher\u2019s high xERA provide the perfect environment for us to hunt for early base paths.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Travis Bazzana**, who hovered in the high-40s but ultimately fell short of the starting cut. While his matchup against the struggling Bratt provides a solid SP Skill boost, his inefficiency against left-handed pitching and a lower lineup slot meant he couldn't surpass the reliability offered by **Henry Bolte** or **Austin Riley**. Elsewhere, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Jose Caballero**; despite a 56.69 score, he faces the formidable Imanaga, and his spot at the bottom of the order forces us to temper expectations. We remain locked into this configuration while monitoring the health of **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, and **Trevor Story**, all of whom remain sidelined, leaving us to rely on our active depth to keep the pressure on our division rivals.",
